handlemap -- can M's ruling be executed from the volumes alone?
==============================================================================

1  THE MAP THE VOLUMES SUPPORT, order-free
   RESOLVED      112 of 265 handles
   AMBIGUOUS      55 of 265 handles
   UNRESOLVED     98 of 265 handles
   and by site in the bibliography's objects column (407 sites over 162 rows):
   RESOLVED      178
   AMBIGUOUS      81
   UNRESOLVED    148
   and in the main volume (76 sites): {'AMBIGUOUS': 33, 'RESOLVED': 28, 'UNRESOLVED': 15}

2  THE ORDERING HYPOTHESIS, REPORTED AS A FINDING AND NOT USED AS A METHOD
   fam   objects  handles  resolutions where position predicts
   3B          9        9  0 of 5   <-- NOT in handle order
   A          43       43  12 of 12
   B          21       21  7 of 7
   C           9        9  3 of 3
   E           4        4  2 of 2
   EM         10        7  -- counts differ, position is not even defined
   F           4        4  2 of 2
   G          12       12  10 of 10
   I           3        3  2 of 2
   K          25       24  -- counts differ, position is not even defined
   L          68       41  -- counts differ, position is not even defined
   LS          8        8  2 of 6   <-- NOT in handle order
   M           9        9  3 of 4   <-- NOT in handle order
   P          17       17  6 of 6
   Q          11       11  6 of 7   <-- NOT in handle order
   S          21       18  -- counts differ, position is not even defined
   T          16       16  5 of 5
   W           9        9  4 of 5   <-- NOT in handle order
   across the equal-count families: 64 agree, 12 do not.
   3B is nine objects and nine handles and its objects are in MEANING order;
   W is nine and nine and is in handle order.  Nothing in the volumes says which
   a family is, so the ordering cannot be used to resolve a single handle.

3  WHAT THE APPENDIX G ANCHORS CONTRIBUTE
   anchors held: 29, over 5 families
   resolutions whose evidence is the handle's own suffix: 110
   resolutions whose evidence is an Appendix G anchor   : 2

4  WHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE RULING
   M ruled that a handle is replaced by the object's descriptive title.
   112 of 265 handles have a title the volumes support.
   55 name several objects and this instrument chooses none.
   98 have no evidence here at all.
   By site, 178 of the bibliography's 407 can be written and 229 cannot.
   THE TABLE IS WRITTEN FOR APPROVAL, NOT APPLIED.
